  "description": "The tool service's methods, by whether they change the plot they name (SUB-25). While an earlier revision of a plot is shown read-only, VS Code refuses every method aimed at that plot that is not in leaves_plot (an allow-list: a method added later is refused until listed), and sends debrief/open with read_only, so an interrupted change is not recovered. Python's WRITING_METHODS and tools/call are changes_plot; every other method it knows is leaves_plot. debrief/export_image records the export in the plot's island, never a step, which an export of an earlier revision may (decision, product owner, 16 Oct 2026). Held by python/debrief-tools/tests/test_figures_service.py and vscode/test/unit/export.test.ts.",
